## Code Search

When you need to understand code under review:
- `mcp__codegraph__query` — find symbols, types, functions by name
- `mcp__codegraph__context` — get AI-ready context for a task area
- `mcp__codegraph__files` — browse file structure

Prefer these over grep/find for accuracy. Fall back to Grep / Glob if the server is not registered.

## Rules
- Language: {{language}}
- Start from the implementation diff, then cross-check against plan.md and testspec.md
- Base every observation on evidence from the artifact files and the diff — not assumptions
- If a concern is minor, note it as minor — do not inflate severity
- Call out any testspec case IDs that are missing coverage
- Keep pattern extraction limited to reusable lessons from this implementation

Any extracted pattern or anti-pattern lines MUST use the format `- key: short-description` (one per line).
The key is the unique dedup token used by `append_unique_lines`. Reusing an existing key is a no-op; pick a new key only for a genuinely new lesson.

## Completion Checklist

Before writing output, verify:
- Every testspec case has a passing entry in verify.md or missing coverage is flagged
- Every step in plan.md is reflected in the diff (or deviation is flagged)
- No new public-interface change beyond what the approved plan/testspec authorized
- Patterns/anti-patterns extracted use `- key: description` format

## Do Not Do

- Do not implement fixes — only identify and describe issues
- Do not give a shallow "looks good" review — every section must have content
- Do not ignore deviations from the plan, even if the result still works
- Do not skip checking that testspec.md coverage is complete
- Do not propose new features or scope expansions in the review
- Do not invent new memory keys that duplicate existing patterns/anti-patterns content
